---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import CategoryChip from '../components/CategoryChip.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../components/NewsletterBlock.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const description =
	'Field notes from Will, Head of Marketing & Customer Experience at a UK education business, on building, marketing, and using AI in practice.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About · ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header current="about" />
		<main>
			<header class="hero">
				<h1>About</h1>
				<div class="byline">
					<strong>Will</strong>
					<span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
					<span>Head of Marketing &amp; CX</span>
					<span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
					<span>UK</span>
				</div>
				<p class="dek">{description}</p>
			</header>

			<section class="prose intro">
				<p>
					I'm Will, Head of Marketing &amp; Customer Experience at a UK education business,
					where I look after a marketing team, a lead generation function, and a customer
					solutions team.
				</p>
				<p>
					Most of what I do day-to-day sits at the intersection of three things: building
					an integrated acquisition and retention model, figuring out how AI actually
					changes marketing (rather than how it's supposed to), and helping a team of
					seven do their best work.
				</p>
				<p>This site is where I write about what I'm learning in the open.</p>
			</section>

			<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
			<p class="prose lead">
				Field Notes is a working notebook, not a thought-leadership outlet. Posts tend to
				fall into three categories:
			</p>

			<div class="categories">
				<div class="cat-block">
					<div class="cat-left">
						<CategoryChip tag="building" size="lg" />
						<a class="fn-link browse" href={`${base}/blog/`}>Browse →</a>
					</div>
					<div class="cat-right">
						<p class="cat-title">Things I'm building</p>
						<p class="cat-body">
							AI tools, internal systems, websites, side projects. I show the work: what I
							tried, what broke, what I'd do differently. Most recently, an AI chatbot for
							our customer-facing site, a weekly meal-planning app built on the Claude API,
							and the site you're reading now.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="cat-block">
					<div class="cat-left">
						<CategoryChip tag="marketing" size="lg" />
						<a class="fn-link browse" href={`${base}/blog/`}>Browse →</a>
					</div>
					<div class="cat-right">
						<p class="cat-title">Marketing thinking</p>
						<p class="cat-body">
							How I'm approaching the work: campaigns, team structure, customer experience,
							the retention/acquisition handoff, the awkward bits no one writes about. Less
							framework-shopping, more "here's what we tried and what happened."
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="cat-block">
					<div class="cat-left">
						<CategoryChip tag="ai" size="lg" />
						<a class="fn-link browse" href={`${base}/blog/`}>Browse →</a>
					</div>
					<div class="cat-right">
						<p class="cat-title">AI, practically</p>
						<p class="cat-body">
							Where it earns its keep in real organisations, where it doesn't, and the gap
							between the demos and the day job. Written for colleagues and peers who are
							bored of the hype and want to know what's actually useful on a Tuesday
							morning.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h2>Who I'm writing for</h2>
			<p class="prose">
				People doing the work, not watching it. Marketers, operators, team leads, anyone
				trying to integrate AI into a real organisation with real constraints. If you're
				senior enough that no one above you knows the answer either, you'll probably find
				something useful here.
			</p>

			<h2>A note on what this isn't</h2>
			<p class="prose">
				I'm not selling anything. I'm not a consultant. I don't have a course. I'm a
				practitioner figuring it out in public, which means I'll be wrong sometimes, and
				I'd rather be wrong out loud than vague in private.
			</p>

			<NewsletterBlock />
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
<style>
	.hero {
		margin-bottom: 44px;
	}
	.hero h1 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: 92px;
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 0.98;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
	}
	.byline {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px;
		margin-top: 24px;
		font-size: 14px;
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
		padding-bottom: 22px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
	}
	.byline strong {
		color: rgb(var(--text));
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.byline .sep {
		opacity: 0.4;
	}
	.dek {
		font-style: italic;
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
		font-size: 22px;
		line-height: 1.45;
		margin: 28px 0 0;
		max-width: 620px;
	}
	.intro {
		max-width: 680px;
	}
	main h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-atkinson);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1;
		margin: 52px 0 18px;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
	}
	.prose.lead {
		max-width: 680px;
	}
	.categories {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 20px;
		margin: 20px 0 24px;
	}
	.cat-block {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr;
		gap: 24px;
		padding: 20px 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
	}
	.cat-left {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 10px;
	}
	.browse {
		font-size: 13px;
	}
	.cat-title {
		font-family: var(--font-atkinson);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 19px;
		color: rgb(var(--text));
		margin: 0 0 8px;
		line-height: 1.25;
		letter-spacing: -0.005em;
	}
	.cat-body {
		color: rgb(var(--text-muted));
		font-size: 17px;
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.55;
		max-width: 560px;
	}
	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.hero {
			margin-bottom: 32px;
		}
		.hero h1 {
			font-size: 54px;
		}
		.dek {
			font-size: 19px;
			margin-top: 22px;
		}
		main h2 {
			font-size: 12px;
			margin: 36px 0 14px;
		}
		.categories {
			gap: 16px;
			margin: 16px 0;
		}
		.cat-block {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 10px;
			padding: 16px 0;
		}
		.cat-title {
			font-size: 17px;
		}
		.cat-body {
			font-size: 16px;
		}
	}
</style>
